# ⚡ LT Line Health Monitoring & Intelligent Safety System

A low-cost, decentralized monitoring system designed to **continuously monitor Low Tension (LT) distribution lines, detect abnormal conditions, and isolate affected sections** using distributed sensor nodes and long-range wireless communication.

---

## 🚧 Overview

Low Tension (LT) distribution lines can develop faults, abnormal loading conditions, or interruptions that may remain undetected until they result in outages, equipment damage, or safety hazards.

This project proposes a **distributed IoT-based monitoring and protection architecture** in which multiple sensor nodes are deployed along an LT distribution line.

Each node continuously monitors electrical parameters and communicates its status wirelessly. When an abnormal condition or node failure is detected, the system can initiate **relay-based isolation of the affected section**.

The design focuses on:

* Low-cost hardware
* Distributed monitoring
* Long-range communication
* Self-powered sensor nodes
* Automatic fault isolation
* Scalable deployment

---

## 🧠 Core Concept

The system uses a network of **plug-and-play monitoring nodes** distributed across an LT line.

Each node:

1. Measures electrical parameters.
2. Processes the measurements using an ESP32.
3. Transmits its status through LoRa.
4. Monitors communication and node health.
5. Controls a relay for section isolation when required.

