## ⚙️ Working Principle

### 🟢 Normal Operation

During normal operation:

```text
LT Line
   ↓
Voltage & Current Sensing
   ↓
ESP32
   ↓
Parameter Processing
   ↓
LoRa Communication
   ↓
Central Monitoring System
```

The sensor node continuously measures electrical parameters and periodically transmits its status.

The system maintains the node as **healthy** as long as the measured parameters and communication status remain within the defined operating conditions.

---

### 🔴 Fault / Abnormal Condition

When an abnormal condition is detected:

```text
Abnormal Condition
        ↓
Sensor Measurement
        ↓
ESP32 Processing
        ↓
Fault Identification
        ↓
Relay Control
        ↓
Affected Section Isolated
```

The system can respond to conditions such as:

* Abnormal voltage
* Abnormal current
* Node communication failure
* Sensor/node inactivity
* Other predefined fault conditions

The isolation mechanism is intended to prevent the affected section from continuing to remain energized.

---

## 🔋 Energy Harvesting & Plug-and-Play Architecture

A key objective of the system is to minimize dependence on external power sources.

The monitoring node is designed to obtain its operating power through **energy harvesting from the monitored line**, reducing the need for dedicated batteries or external supplies.

This enables:

* Reduced installation complexity
* Lower maintenance requirements
* Easier deployment across multiple locations
* Modular replacement of sensor nodes
* Improved scalability

> ⚠️ The prototype currently uses an external low-voltage supply. Energy-harvesting based powering is part of the intended system architecture.

